# This repo is PUBLIC and serves GitHub Pages from the branch root, so anything
# committed here is published. It had no ignore rules at all, and an experimental
# project sitting in a subdirectory left a Firebase service-account key and a
# .env.local in the working tree — one `git add -A` away from being public.
# Nothing leaked (neither was ever committed), but the guard belongs here.

# Credentials — never publishable, under any path.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/serviceAccountKey.json
**/*-service-account*.json
**/serviceAccount*.json

# Build output and dependencies from any experiment dropped in here.
node_modules/
.cache/
*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store
